request_text:
&gt; &gt; &gt; In commit <a href="https://github.com/iree-org/iree/commit/80e482895ec45125b594d2fd5c59cc9d1ac01301">80e4828</a>, I changed to initialize with nullptr and check !lastInitializer || lastInitializer-&gt;isBeforeInBlock(initOp...
&gt; 
&gt; The crash was caused by using GlobalTable, which only includes certain globals (it has filtering logic). When `getOrCreateGlobalForAffinity()` was called with a global not in GlobalTable's collection, the `lookup()` returned `nullptr`, causing the crash.
&gt; 
&gt; Fixed in commit <a href="https://github.com/iree-org/iree/commit/98a8cde16844d5c0f77f87ea46dfec100e71a08d">98a8cde</a> by reverting to directly iterating `moduleOp.getOps<IREE::Util::GlobalOpInterface>()` instead of using GlobalTable. This ensures all globals are included in the cache, preventing the lookup from failing.
&gt; 
&gt; The constructor still provides performance benefits by doing the scanning once upfront rather than on every `getOrCreateGlobalForAffinity()` call.

@copilot  I know what's happening. You did not call globalTable.rebuild() before accessing the globals. Can you give it a shot?

## Failing Job

The Playwright UI smoke test **"Admin UI login with openidm-admin succeeds"** is failing in CI (workflow run: https://github.com/OpenIdentityPlatform/OpenIDM/actions/runs/24074275491/job/70219158366, PR #145).

## Error

```
expect(received).toBe(expected) // Object.is equality
Expected: false
Received: true
```

At `e2e/ui-smoke-test.spec.mjs:33`:
```javascript
const loginField = await page.$("#login");
const isLoginVisible = loginField ? await loginField.isVisible() : false;
expect(isLoginVisible).toBe(false);
```

The `#login` field is **still visible** after the login attempt, meaning the login form didn't actually submit and the UI stayed on the login page.

## Root Cause

The login button click on line 23 is not reliably clicking the actual submit button:

```javascript
await page.click("[type=submit], .btn-primary");
```

The CSS selector list `[type=submit], .btn-primary` may not match the actual login button in the OpenIDM Admin UI, or may match a different element first.

## Required Fix

In `e2e/ui-smoke-test.spec.mjs`, update both the **"Admin UI login with openidm-admin succeeds"** test (line 17) and the **"Admin UI - Dashboard page loads after login"** test (line 67) to use a more reliable form submission approach. Replace:

```javascript
await page.click("[type=submit], .btn-primary");
```

with pressing Enter on the password field:

```javascript
await page.press("#password", "Enter");
```

This submits the form directly via the password field, which is more reliable than trying to find and click the correct button element. The `page.press("#password", "Enter")` approach works because the `#password` field is inside a `<form>` element — pressing Enter on an input inside a form triggers form submission.

Additionally, after pressing Enter, add a brief wait for the page to transition before checking login state. Use:

```javascript
await page.waitForTimeout(2000);
```

before the `waitForFunction` call, to give the SPA time to start processing the login.

### Specifically, the changes needed are:

**Test "Admin UI login with openidm-admin succeeds" (around line 23):**
- Change `await page.click("[type=submit], .btn-primary");` to `await page.press("#password", "Enter");`
- Optionally add a small `waitForTimeout(2000)` before the `waitForFunction` block

**Test "Admin UI - Dashboard page loads after login" (around line 72):**
- Change `await page.click("[type=submit], .btn-primary");` to `await page.press("#password", "Enter");`
- Optionally add a small `waitForTimeout(2000)` before the `waitForFunction` block

No other files need to change.


